---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import PageIntro from '../components/site/PageIntro.astro';
import { COMPANY_NAME, SECURITY_CONTACT_EMAIL } from '../data/company';

const LAST_UPDATED = '2026-10-20';
---

<Layout
  title={`Responsible Disclosure | ${COMPANY_NAME}`}
  description="How to report a security vulnerability in the ByteLite LLC website."
  path="/responsible-disclosure"
  noindex={true}
>
  <PageIntro eyebrow="Security" heading="Responsible disclosure">
    <p class="small-print">Last updated <time datetime={LAST_UPDATED}>20 October 2026</time>.</p>
  </PageIntro>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap prose legal">
      <h2>Scope</h2>
      <p>This policy covers security issues affecting:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>The website at thebytelite.com, including every page it serves.</li>
        <li>The contact form and the server function behind it.</li>
        <li>The checkout and billing endpoints of this website, which are currently switched off.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Private software, research systems and non-public infrastructure are outside the scope of
        public testing unless {COMPANY_NAME} authorizes it in writing.
      </p>
      <p>
        Do not test payment flows with real card details. Describe a suspected payment issue and it
        will be reproduced in a test environment.
      </p>

      <h2>How to report</h2>
      <p>
        Email <a href={`mailto:${SECURITY_CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{SECURITY_CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>, or use the
        <a href="/contact">contact form</a>. Include a description of the issue, steps to reproduce it,
        its likely impact and how to reach you.
      </p>

      <h2>What to expect</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>A reasonable effort to acknowledge valid reports and keep you informed.</li>
        <li>An explanation of what was found, including when an issue is judged not exploitable.</li>
        <li>Credit when the issue is resolved, if you want it.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        {COMPANY_NAME} is a founder-led company with no security team on call, so there is no guaranteed
        response time. A real vulnerability in a live path is handled ahead of other work.
      </p>

      <h2>Please do not</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Access or change data that is not yours.</li>
        <li>Take any action that could harm the service or its users, including denial-of-service testing.</li>
        <li>Disclose the issue publicly before it has been addressed.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Good-faith research</h2>
      <p>
        {COMPANY_NAME} will not pursue legal action against researchers who follow this policy, act in
        good faith and cause no harm.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .legal ul { padding-left: 1.25rem; display: grid; gap: var(--space-2); color: var(--color-ink-muted); }
</style>
